    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from favorable matchups against Brandon Young and Trey Yesavage, respectively. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is our premier start; his high xwOBA (0.378) paired with a +16% park factor elevation makes him a high-ceiling play despite the moderate xERA of his opposing starter. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.88) and **Josh Jung** (60.98) provide solid secondary support. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** in particular benefits from a 14% platoon boost against the right-handed Michael King, while **Josh Jung** leverages a favorable +11% skill adjustment against Seth Lugo to crack the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold.\n\nWhile we are chasing points, our mandate to prioritize SB efficiency keeps **Nasim Nunez** (49.35) and **Andy Pages** (48.06) in the conversation despite lower raw outputs. **Nasim Nunez** draws a tough assignment against Michael King, and his output is heavily suppressed by an 8% penalty for hitting in the #9 hole, yet his elite speed profile remains a strategic necessity. The closest call on the bench was **Coby Mayo** (46.80), whose 16% park adjustment nearly pushed him over the mark. Ultimately, the optimizer favored the platoon advantages of **Miguel Andujar** (55.79) and **Dominic Smith** (55.13) against left-handed starters, as their respective efficiency profiles provided a safer floor for today's roster caps.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, as the scores for **Liam Hicks**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill** are all subject to volatility if they shift in the batting order. **Kyle Tucker** (52.36) faces a stiff test against Jes\u00fas Luzardo\u2019s elite arm, resulting in a significant 18% skill-based deduction. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** faces a negative 13% platoon adjustment against Foster Griffin. We are effectively betting that volume and roster necessity outweigh these matchup risks today; should any of these players drop further down the order, we will be forced to reconsider their status to preserve our game caps.",
